mod:list_ptr_write_rootless_base;
// A WRITE THROUGH A POINTER WHOSE LAST POINTER BASE HAS NO NAMED ROOT IS JUDGED (DEF-615, landing 177d2b3). A growth handed `(raw idhp(q)).lp` or `(o ??! E5).lp`
// writes the `List` behind a pointer member read straight off a call's result or an unwrap. `check_pointer_targets` (alias.npk) took that call or unwrap as the
// write's pointer base, the named arm's `path_steps` can't spell a base with no named root, and nobody judged the write: `int64->:e = raw fp(q.lp);
// discard(raw growh((raw idhp(q)).lp)); pass <-e;` read freed heap on main and on every build before this row. Now a pointer base with no named root is no base:
// the place is resolved by rule A (`escape_pointer_targets`), as a bare call's result is. Each module is one cell; each fault cell takes `e = raw fp(q.lp)` (or the
// family's spelling), grows the same `List` and reads `e`. `…l` is a cell's local twin (the struct a local over a local `H`, the pointer to it a local).
// CLOSED HERE, 25: `zv10` `growh((raw idhp(q)).lp)`; `zv1` `(o ??! E5).lp` as the take and the growth over `HP->?:o`; `zv2` the take through a bound local, the growth
// through the unwrap; `zv5` `(r ?! E5).lp` over `Result<HP->>:r`; `zv6` `(q.o ??! E5).lp`; `zg10` `(<-(raw idhp(q))).lp`; `zg12d` `list_push(@((<-((raw idhp(q)).lp)).l), …)`;
// `zg14` a pointer receiver, `((raw idhp(q)).lp).grow()`; `zg14u` `((o ??! E5).lp).grow()`; `zg15` the whole pointee assigned, `<-((raw idhp(q)).lp) = raw mkh();`;
// `zg17` `(is (c) : q : (raw idhp(q))).lp`; `zg18` `((raw idhp(q)) =>! HP->).lp`; each with its local twin; and `zu4f`, `zv1`'s twin over an `HV` that owns a `List`.
// REFUSED BEFORE THIS ROW, the same families' yardsticks: `zv1p` the plain `q.lp` (from DEF-584); `zv3` the take through the unwrap; `zv4` the unwrap bound; `zv7`
// `o?.lp ??! E5` (DEF-601); `zv8` the growth through a bound copy; `zv9` through an identity's result; `zg13d` `@((<-(raw idh(q.lp))).l)` (DEF-309's own); `zg14p`
// the plain receiver; `zg15p` the plain pointee assigned; `zg16` a ternary of two members; each with its local twin. A named pointer's write stays the named arm's.
// TWO RIGHT PROGRAMS ARE REFUSED HERE, DEF-616's FACES (`…_price616`; LOW, fails closed, made by this row, open): a pointer place with no named root REASSIGNED under a
// live holder is judged as a write through the pointer's old value. `zr1`: `int64->:e = raw fp(q.lp); (<-(raw idhp(q))).lp = other; pass (<-e) + 6i64;`; `zr2`:
// `<-(raw idhh(pp)) = other;` with an element of the old pointee held. Re-pointing frees nothing. The named spelling keeps the reading that the pointer moves and the
// pointee is left alone, and rule A doesn't.
// Their plain twins `zr1p` (`q.lp = other;`), `zr1d` (`(<-q).lp = other;`) and `zr2p` (`<-pp = other;`) are refused since DEF-584, where their local twins compile:
// DEF-614's faces (`…_price614`; LOW, fails closed, open).
